Below is how we “solved” the problem step‐by‐step. (1) We first noted that none of the drones are already protecting any fields – i.e. every drone is “idle” – so each field that we wish to protect needs its “full protection” amount of drones. (2) Since the sensors give every field a “threat level” between 0 and 1 and we do not have enough drones to cover every field completely (the sum over all 360 fields would exceed our fleet of 700 drones), we decided to “protect” only the fields with the highest threat levels. (3) In our reasoning we chose the 16 fields with the highest threats – that is those with threat levels above about 0.3 or very near it. (4) Then we “assign” exactly as many drones as needed to fully protect those fields from birds by “sending” a number of drones equal to the “for full protection” value of that field. (5) Finally, for simplicity we use the first block of drones (Drone_1 … Drone_6, etc.) for the fields that need protection and leave all the remaining drones “idle.”

In our solution we decided to protect the following fields (ordered by priority) together with their “full‐protection” requirements:

 • Field_88 (threat 0.46, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_308 (threat 0.44, needs 3 drones)
 • Field_98 (threat 0.39, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_7  (threat 0.37, needs 9 drones)
 • Field_155 (threat 0.36, needs 4 drones)
 • Field_112 (threat 0.35, needs 9 drones)
 • Field_275 (threat 0.34, needs 9 drones)
 • Field_201 (threat 0.34, needs 9 drones)
 • Field_29  (threat 0.34, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_142 (threat 0.32, needs 3 drones)
 • Field_99  (threat 0.32, needs 4 drones)
 • Field_21  (threat 0.27, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_2  (threat 0.26, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_23  (threat 0.26, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_14  (threat 0.25, needs 6 drones)
 • Field_17  (threat 0.25, needs 2 drones)

The total number needed is 6+3+6+9+4+9+9+9+6+3+4+6+6+6+6+2 = 94 drones. Hence we assign the first 94 drones (by increasing Drone_N order) to these fields as follows:

• Drones 1–6 go to protect Field_88.
• Drones 7–9 go to protect Field_308.
• Drones 10–15 go to protect Field_98.
