The “assignment” we have chosen is simply to stick with the “mounted” target field that already appears on the drone’s descriptor (if it is “moving_to_field” or “protecting”) so that its final group is “protecting Field_<name>” (using exactly the target field provided) and to leave every drone that is “idle” assigned to the “idle” group. (In other words, every drone that is already “in‐action” remains on its “protecting…” assignment and every drone that is not already engaged remains idle.) 

For example, Field_88 needs full security so the drones already assigned there (Drone_1 through Drone_6) continue with group “protecting Field_88”. Field_7 is full with its nine drones (five already protecting and four “moving_to_field”), so those drones keep their current assignment (“protecting Field_7”), and so on. All the drones that are idle remain “idle.”

The final group‐assignment for each drone is therefore determined “as is” by checking the drone’s state:
– If its state is “moving_to_field” or “protecting” (with some target field), then its final group is “protecting <target field>”.
– If its state is “idle” then its final group is “idle.”

